[00:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Is this real or AI generated? Sometimes it can be difficult to tell. For hundreds of years, humans have used watermarks to prove where content was created. One challenge is developing a mark that\'s hidden to viewers, but'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'visible to those looking for it. Enter SynthID by Google DeepMind. It can produce a digital watermark that\'s imperceptible to humans and works across Google products to tag AI generated'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'images, video, audio, and text. The watermark can withstand common editing techniques like reordering and trimming, adding noise, compression,'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cropping, and filters. How? For images, it can be embedded directly into the pixels. For video, it also marks every frame. For audio, SynthID converts the signal'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'into a spectrogram, a visual representation of the sound waves, into which it embeds the watermark before it converts everything back into a waveform.'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For text, SynthID looks at which words are going to be generated next and changes the probability for suitable word choices that wouldn\'t affect the overall text quality and utility. If a passage contains more instances of'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'preferred word choices, SynthID will detect that it\'s watermarked. You can\'t read, hear, or see the watermarks, so you can fully enjoy your creations. SynthID technology is already used'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'across generative AI Google consumer products. SynthID is just one tool we\'re using to make sure generative AI tools are built with safety in mind from the beginning, empowering people and organizations to'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'create responsibly.'
